BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mahjong For Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T143000
UID:6a6d54269006f75353142e15@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn\, play\, connect\, and meet new friends through Mahjong
 —perfect for beginners and experienced players. Includes a quick intro a
 nd friendly gameplay. No experience needed.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6d54269006f75353142e15
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Podcasting 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260903T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260903T190000
UID:6a3b084c296ea565de2e52c5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all young adults!\nDid you know 'podcast' comes from i
 Pod and broadcast? This intro session will include fun facts about the evo
 lution of podcasting\, an interactive listening component and best practic
 es when making your own podcast. You’ll walk away being able to speak co
 nfidently about the medium and learn about the making of some of your favo
 urite shows. You’ll also have the foundational information needed to sta
 rt your own show!\nNo experience necessary.\nDrop-in!\nHosted by Amanda Cu
 pido\, an award-winning podcast producer\, university instructor\, former 
 TPL Innovator in Residence\, and author of\nLet's Talk Podcasting: The Ess
 ential Guide to Doing it Right\n!
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3b084c296ea565de2e52c5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Knit\, Crochet & Crafting Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T150000
UID:69741154d2bbe265eb298813@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bring your own knit\, crochet\, or other portable craft proje
 ct\, and hang out and chat with other crafters while you work!
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69741154d2bbe265eb298813
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Board Games for Adults: Wednesday Afternoon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T160000
UID:69a204c61e64afd01e5e9197@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the fun of playing modern and classic board games!
 \nDrop in with your friends (or make some new ones) and play games like:\n
 Anomia\, Backgammon\, Bananagrams\, Chess\, CodeNames\, Connect Four\, Ex
 ploding Kittens\, Monopoly\, Quirkle\, Rumikub\, Scrabble\, Set\, Settlers
  of Catan\, Snakes and Ladders\, Sorry\, SushiGO\, UNO\, UpWords and ma
 ny more!\nPlease don't hesitate to call us or visit the red desk on the fi
 rst floor if you have any questions.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a204c61e64afd01e5e9197
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The SciFi and Fantasy Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T160000
UID:6a209046bd892a0672e787ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the book club hosted by The Merril Collection of S
 cience Fiction\, Speculation & Fantasy. Each month we will read a book fro
 m a different sub-genre such as space opera\, high fantasy\, cyberpunk and
  more.\nOur September title is\nRed Team Blues\nby Cory Doctorow.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Merril Collection Reading Room\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a209046bd892a0672e787ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Friday Crafts - Air Dry Clay!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260814T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260814T153000
UID:6a580165fb418a28009b3d36@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:It's easy and fun to sculpt cute little figurines from colourf
 ul air dry clay! We'll have a variety of colours of clay and some simple i
 nstructions to help you make wonderful little keepsakes.\nOther activities
 \, such as colouring and board games\, are always available at our Friday
  Crafts sessions. Come have fun and meet some new people from your communi
 ty!\nDrop in.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a580165fb418a28009b3d36
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Friday - Anne of Green Gables
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T153000
UID:6a32e9482ea730c17ab7a54a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a variety of diverse films! July:\nAnne of Green G
 ables.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Wychwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a32e9482ea730c17ab7a54a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing with Structure: An Introduction to Box Drawing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T200000
UID:6a5e64ba3896acb13e3f8d6f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Learn the basic idea of structural drawing\, a technique co
 mmonly used by artists and designers to sketch objects more accurately in 
 this introductory hands on workshop. Learn how to simplify objects into ba
 sic geometric forms—especially boxes—and use light construction lines 
 to understand proportion and structure. Through a short demonstration and 
 guided practice\, participants will experiment with drawing everyday objec
 ts using this practical method.\nMaterials will be provided.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Floor 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e64ba3896acb13e3f8d6f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
